WEBVTT

00:12.370 --> 00:15.730
Rhaenys, I'd like to discuss
something with you.

00:15.730 --> 00:17.430
I have nothing to say.

00:17.430 --> 00:19.480
I told you to stay away from me.

00:19.820 --> 00:22.720
You're looking for Yuke Feldio,
are you not?

00:23.290 --> 00:26.460
It's not as if there's no
way to find him at all.

00:26.460 --> 00:27.990
What are you saying?

00:27.990 --> 00:31.490
(Seeker's Compass)
Are you familiar with an artifact
called the Seeker's Compass?

00:32.580 --> 00:38.280
Yes! It's a compass that reveals the
location of anything its user seeks.

00:38.280 --> 00:41.730
From hidden treasures
to missing persons...

00:41.730 --> 00:42.830
Anything.

00:42.830 --> 00:44.170
You have one?

00:44.170 --> 00:45.260
No...

00:45.610 --> 00:48.620
Though I do know someone who might.

00:48.620 --> 00:50.020
Tell me!

00:50.020 --> 00:53.270
Is that how you ask someone for a favor?

00:55.600 --> 00:57.270
Please tell me who has it.

00:58.760 --> 01:01.520
Prince Mastoma has the compass.

01:02.580 --> 01:05.450
You can negotiate with him
for it yourself.

01:05.450 --> 01:09.970
If you can avoid offending him,
he might lend it to you.

01:10.530 --> 01:13.680
But if you don't believe me,

01:13.680 --> 01:14.910
then we're done here.

01:15.650 --> 01:19.920
Have fun waiting for the
Adventurer's Guild to find his body.

01:20.640 --> 01:23.080
All right. I'll go.

01:24.250 --> 01:26.770
Both the prince and I are busy men.

01:26.770 --> 01:28.200
We will depart at once.

01:28.200 --> 01:29.180
Right now?

01:29.180 --> 01:33.540
We nobles don't have all the
time in the world, you know.

01:33.540 --> 01:35.660
And the man we're seeing is royalty.

01:35.660 --> 01:38.310
An audience with him requires
certain procedures.

01:39.190 --> 01:42.220
Fine. I'll go with you.

01:42.220 --> 01:44.890
You're worried about your friends,
aren't you?

01:44.890 --> 01:47.320
Write them a letter in the carriage.

01:47.320 --> 01:49.060
I'll have it sent to their lodging.

01:53.850 --> 01:55.580
Yuke Feldio...

01:55.580 --> 01:57.560
If you're lucky enough to
have your corpse found,

01:57.560 --> 02:00.010
I'll buy some flowers
to put on your grave...

02:00.010 --> 02:03.580
with the money I make selling your woman!

02:14.140 --> 02:21.100
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

03:36.220 --> 03:41.800
(Episode 16:
Return From the Twilight, And...)

03:41.800 --> 03:44.940
"Achromatic Darkness" sure
turned out to be an apt name.

03:44.940 --> 03:47.580
No matter how far I go,
I can't see a thing.

03:47.580 --> 03:48.730
Nothing changes.

03:49.040 --> 03:53.000
I can't even tell if I'm
making progress, falling,

03:53.000 --> 03:55.240
or just standing still.

03:59.720 --> 04:01.000
Yuke...

04:03.670 --> 04:04.500
Rain?

04:09.090 --> 04:10.540
What's that?

04:10.540 --> 04:12.010
A light...

04:12.370 --> 04:13.820
It's probably the exit.

04:13.820 --> 04:15.340
You can tell?

04:15.340 --> 04:18.010
No, but it feels like it.

04:19.070 --> 04:20.000
Shall we?

04:20.660 --> 04:21.400
Yeah.

04:27.570 --> 04:30.000
Hold on tight, Rune.

04:30.000 --> 04:30.890
Okay.

05:00.340 --> 05:02.260
You okay, Rune?

05:02.990 --> 05:04.310
Wasn't expecting that...

05:13.880 --> 05:15.820
I'll start a fire, okay?

05:18.230 --> 05:19.690
It's so warm.

05:19.690 --> 05:21.140
I feel alive again.

05:21.140 --> 05:25.080
I'm glad we made it out of there alive.

05:25.080 --> 05:27.390
Let's get moving once our clothes are dry.

05:27.390 --> 05:29.580
Where do you suppose we are?

05:29.880 --> 05:32.590
I recognize the shape of that mountain.

05:32.590 --> 05:36.280
I'm pretty sure this river is
one that flows out of Lake Ryne.

05:36.280 --> 05:39.260
If it is, Duna can't be that far away.

05:39.260 --> 05:41.720
Once we find the road, we should
be able to hail a stagecoach.

05:42.070 --> 05:45.220
Yeah! Let's get back to the girls!

05:45.750 --> 05:48.980
Yeah. I can't wait to see everyone.

05:57.410 --> 06:01.620
Everyone! It's Yuke and Rune!
They've returned!

06:01.910 --> 06:04.920
We finally made it. Way to go.

06:04.920 --> 06:06.670
I'm so tired.

06:06.670 --> 06:09.300
You need a good night's sleep
in a warm bed.

06:12.350 --> 06:14.770
We're back, and Rune's safe.

06:14.770 --> 06:16.370
Yuke! Rune!

06:16.370 --> 06:17.079
H-Hey...

06:17.080 --> 06:18.010
- Thank goodness!
- H-Hey...

06:18.010 --> 06:19.760
That hurts...

06:19.760 --> 06:21.010
Oh, sorry!

06:21.010 --> 06:22.700
I'm so glad you're safe!

06:22.700 --> 06:24.390
We were worried, you know!

06:24.840 --> 06:26.940
Y-Yeah... Thanks.

06:26.940 --> 06:29.600
But don't you think this is a bit much?

06:29.600 --> 06:32.650
What are you talking about?!
You were gone for two weeks!

06:32.650 --> 06:33.150
Huh?

06:33.420 --> 06:36.400
You have no idea how worried we were!

06:36.720 --> 06:38.220
Two weeks?

06:39.460 --> 06:45.790
They've been so worried about you
and Rune that they couldn't sleep.

06:46.110 --> 06:49.400
I thought it had been
half a day at most...

06:49.400 --> 06:51.460
Yeah. What's going on?

06:51.720 --> 06:52.700
Half a day?

06:52.700 --> 06:53.960
It was two weeks!

06:54.250 --> 06:58.090
So was time itself distorted
in Achromatic Darkness?

06:58.090 --> 07:03.750
That's right. Simon crossed hundreds
or even thousands of years, too.

07:03.750 --> 07:07.970
Does that mean... a thousand years
could have gone by just as easily?

07:08.340 --> 07:09.550
I'm sorry.

07:11.410 --> 07:12.260
Yeah...

07:13.210 --> 07:17.860
But still... I'm so, so relieved
that you're all right.

07:19.420 --> 07:21.860
Sorry I made you two worry.

07:23.090 --> 07:24.930
You weren't scared, were you?

07:24.930 --> 07:28.430
I was okay because I had Yuke.

07:28.430 --> 07:29.620
That's true.

07:30.200 --> 07:32.710
Thank you, Fina.

07:32.710 --> 07:33.620
Not at all.

07:34.110 --> 07:36.880
So, um... where are Rain and Nene?

07:38.120 --> 07:41.360
Rune, you must be tired. Come rest inside.

07:41.360 --> 07:42.380
O-Okay.

07:42.750 --> 07:44.890
I'll arrange some snacks for you.

07:44.890 --> 07:47.630
Oh, yeah! Let's make pancakes!

07:47.970 --> 07:49.190
Yay!

07:49.190 --> 07:50.930
Did something happen?

07:50.930 --> 07:54.150
Actually... Rain's been gone for two days.

07:54.150 --> 07:55.020
What?!

07:55.020 --> 07:57.900
And we just received this.

07:58.950 --> 08:00.740
It's Rain's handwriting.

08:00.740 --> 08:03.710
"I might be able to find out
where Yuke is.

08:03.710 --> 08:06.910
I'm going away for a while. Don't worry."

08:07.380 --> 08:08.760
Who delivered this?

08:08.760 --> 08:11.670
Someone claiming to be a
messenger from Bran Crowder.

08:11.670 --> 08:12.910
That guy?!

08:13.270 --> 08:15.110
They said Rain wouldn't be coming back,

08:15.110 --> 08:19.960
and if we want to talk to her, we should go
to Mastoma's mansion in the center of Duna.

08:19.960 --> 08:22.210
We didn't know what to do.

08:22.920 --> 08:26.430
You've really been working
hard while I was away.

08:26.430 --> 08:27.740
Thanks.

08:27.740 --> 08:31.180
As the leader of Clover,
I'll take over now.

08:31.530 --> 08:33.030
Master...

08:33.030 --> 08:35.560
I'm going to go get Rain.

08:35.560 --> 08:39.440
But aren't you tired?
Maybe you should rest a bit first...

08:39.800 --> 08:43.950
I'll get plenty of rest
after I bring Rain home.

08:44.300 --> 08:48.750
All right. Nene has gone
on ahead to scout the area.

08:48.750 --> 08:50.450
Meet her there.

08:50.840 --> 08:53.960
Okay. I'll bring Rain back.
You can count on it.

08:54.280 --> 08:55.460
Be back soon!

08:55.800 --> 08:58.060
Please be careful.

09:03.530 --> 09:05.720
If you're planning to break in, I'll help.

09:05.990 --> 09:06.810
Nene!

09:06.810 --> 09:10.470
I'm so happy to see you again after two weeks,
I'd like to just leap at you,

09:10.470 --> 09:13.200
but I'll save it for my Nene time.

09:13.200 --> 09:14.350
Sure.

09:14.350 --> 09:16.430
I just said I'm putting it off.

09:16.430 --> 09:18.230
I'm doing my best to hold back here.

09:18.600 --> 09:19.770
Sorry.

09:20.200 --> 09:21.740
Where is it the least guarded?

09:21.740 --> 09:24.020
The guards are solid everywhere.

09:24.020 --> 09:26.860
Then we'll just have to walk right in.

09:30.280 --> 09:32.020
Yuke Feldio?

09:33.050 --> 09:35.870
Have orders to let pass. This way.

09:36.210 --> 09:37.000
Huh?

09:37.000 --> 09:38.870
You wait here.

09:39.710 --> 09:42.190
All right. I'll be back.

09:42.190 --> 09:43.630
Be careful.

09:50.720 --> 09:52.560
It's a pleasure to meet you.

09:52.560 --> 09:56.980
I am Yuke Feldio of the A-rank
party, Clover, from Welmelia.

09:56.980 --> 09:58.350
This is taking too long.

09:58.350 --> 10:00.020
Just speak Welmelian.

10:01.740 --> 10:04.860
How about you tell me why
you're here, Yuke Feldio?

10:05.500 --> 10:07.490
I'm here to take Rain back.

10:07.840 --> 10:11.220
You disrespect the Second
Prince of Salmutaria.

10:11.220 --> 10:13.990
You make it sound as if I
stole something from you.

10:13.990 --> 10:16.250
But, Your Highness, you took Rain—

10:16.250 --> 10:19.750
That woman came to me herself.

10:21.560 --> 10:22.500
Yuke?

10:25.140 --> 10:26.130
Rain?

10:26.870 --> 10:28.440
Yuke!

10:28.440 --> 10:29.260
Go on.

10:31.640 --> 10:32.510
Yuke!

10:33.200 --> 10:35.450
You're back! You're back!

10:35.980 --> 10:37.770
I'm back, Rain.

10:38.250 --> 10:39.520
Rhaenys.

10:40.740 --> 10:42.450
You've won our bet.

10:42.450 --> 10:44.220
You are an intrepid woman.

10:44.220 --> 10:46.400
I truly regret my failure
to make you mine.

10:48.030 --> 10:48.900
Bet?

10:49.210 --> 10:54.200
That woman put her very life
on the line to challenge me.

10:54.200 --> 10:57.910
She said that if you were dead,
she would be mine.

10:58.330 --> 10:59.990
Rain, how could you do that?!

10:59.990 --> 11:02.420
Because I knew you'd be okay!

11:02.750 --> 11:07.520
So long as you're alive,
I can't make her mine, anyway.

11:07.520 --> 11:10.680
That was a dirty trick, Warlock.

11:11.000 --> 11:14.930
I heard it was important to Salmutarians.

11:15.650 --> 11:16.930
Very shrewd.

11:17.220 --> 11:20.530
What do you mean, you can't pay me?!

11:20.530 --> 11:22.060
Y-You!

11:22.370 --> 11:25.070
Yuke Feldio! Weren't you dead?!

11:25.070 --> 11:27.820
Unfortunately for you, I'm alive and well.

11:28.080 --> 11:31.320
Bran, you deceived me.

11:31.320 --> 11:33.200
C-Certainly not!

11:33.200 --> 11:37.330
Rhaenys is the property of Yuke Feldio.

11:37.330 --> 11:39.450
But that's ridiculous!

11:39.450 --> 11:42.600
She told me so herself,
so I looked into it.

11:42.600 --> 11:47.120
There are public records identifying
Rhaenys as Yuke Feldio's property.

11:47.560 --> 11:49.960
Yes. I belong to Yuke.

11:50.320 --> 11:55.240
On top of that, he is currently
an A-rank adventurer of Welmelia,

11:55.240 --> 11:57.470
and he bears the title of hero.

11:57.470 --> 11:59.470
H-Hero?!

11:59.470 --> 12:03.000
Which means it is no
exaggeration to say he is

12:03.000 --> 12:06.840
the personal property of
King Vincent V of Welmelia.

12:06.840 --> 12:10.680
You falsely declared property of
Welmelia's king to be your own

12:10.680 --> 12:13.890
and attempted to sell it
illegally to another nation.

12:15.330 --> 12:19.120
You will pay for the crime
of humiliating me.

12:21.370 --> 12:23.930
Torture him and throw him out.

12:23.930 --> 12:25.500
He's interfering in our discussion.

12:25.500 --> 12:26.300
Yes, Your Highness.

12:27.000 --> 12:32.130
Y-Your Highness! I had no idea!
I-It's the truth!

12:33.080 --> 12:34.380
Please spare me!

12:34.380 --> 12:38.640
As a member of Salmutaria's
royal line, I cannot bow to you,

12:38.640 --> 12:41.140
but I do apologize, Yuke Feldio.

12:41.560 --> 12:46.770
No, Your Highness. I appreciate your
consideration for Rain's safety.

12:48.110 --> 12:51.190
You are blessed with
a good husband, Rhaenys.

12:51.190 --> 12:52.150
Yes.

12:52.480 --> 12:54.830
Still, what a dilemma.

12:54.830 --> 12:55.910
What dilemma?

12:56.200 --> 12:59.800
I'm sure Yuke would be happy to help.

13:01.020 --> 13:04.660
I would like to conquer a dungeon.

13:04.970 --> 13:06.530
A dungeon?

13:06.530 --> 13:10.420
The battle for succession in
Salmutaria has intensified.

13:10.420 --> 13:15.490
If I am to become king, I must
demonstrate my skills in a visible manner.

13:15.490 --> 13:16.540
Uh-huh...

13:16.540 --> 13:20.680
I'm sure you've heard that there
are no dungeons in Salmutaria, yes?

13:21.110 --> 13:23.680
I've heard that it's a very stable place.

13:24.010 --> 13:28.000
Outsiders are told that there
are no dungeons in Salmutaria,

13:28.000 --> 13:30.060
but that's a lie.

13:30.750 --> 13:31.440
Sorry?

13:31.930 --> 13:33.900
I said it's a lie.

13:33.900 --> 13:36.520
There is a dungeon in Salmutaria.

13:36.520 --> 13:38.070
My ancestors shrouded it in secrecy.

13:38.070 --> 13:43.990
Your Highness, if it's that important,
I'll pretend I never heard a—

13:43.990 --> 13:48.580
My plan is to conquer the dungeon and
claim it as a personal achievement.

13:49.150 --> 13:50.710
Welp, I heard it.

13:51.440 --> 13:55.340
However, there are no true
adventurers in my country.

13:56.170 --> 13:58.170
So you wanted Rain to help?

13:58.170 --> 14:01.100
You needed her as an adventurer?

14:02.280 --> 14:04.440
The dungeon has gone
unsupervised for a long time.

14:04.440 --> 14:06.300
It was simply kept a secret.

14:06.300 --> 14:08.010
I don't know the reason,

14:08.010 --> 14:12.730
but I suspect there's something in it with a
connection to the Salmutarian royal blood.

14:13.310 --> 14:17.490
Such as, perhaps, the
Scepter of True Kingship.

14:17.800 --> 14:19.360
The Scepter of True Kingship?

14:19.360 --> 14:23.120
In my country, royal succession is
determined by one's achievements.

14:23.480 --> 14:25.900
But around a dozen generations ago,

14:25.900 --> 14:30.370
it was recorded that the Scepter
of True Kingship decided it.

14:30.370 --> 14:33.500
The dungeon was concealed
around the same time.

14:36.340 --> 14:38.220
Call this a part of my apology.

14:38.220 --> 14:41.390
I needed to explain to you
why I wanted Rhaenys.

14:42.430 --> 14:45.140
Why us, Your Highness?

14:45.450 --> 14:49.230
I heard Clover was one of Welmelia's
most accomplished parties.

14:49.230 --> 14:53.750
Also, that Bran fool said you'd be
a useful asset in many situations.

14:53.750 --> 14:54.970
That's not what I mean.

14:55.520 --> 14:59.750
Even if you had us on your side,
there would be no trust between us.

14:59.750 --> 15:00.780
So why?

15:01.080 --> 15:04.280
You girls have dedicated
yourselves to this Warlock, haven't you?

15:04.280 --> 15:07.540
That's because we like Yuke.

15:09.660 --> 15:16.040
Darling, Welmelian women have their own
will and rights, just like their husbands.

15:16.040 --> 15:18.660
Mejarna!
Why didn't you tell me that sooner?

15:18.660 --> 15:21.430
I explained it many times.

15:21.430 --> 15:24.010
If you want to reform your country,

15:24.010 --> 15:26.930
you ought to listen to your wife more.

15:30.730 --> 15:34.060
Hmph! You won't be laughing
for long, I promise you!

15:34.420 --> 15:36.070
You'll feel the same soon enough.

15:36.490 --> 15:38.210
R-Right...

15:40.280 --> 15:42.820
I'll head back first
and inform the others!

15:42.820 --> 15:44.070
Thanks! I appreciate it!

15:46.650 --> 15:48.130
What should we do?

15:48.130 --> 15:49.620
That's a good question.

15:50.200 --> 15:51.960
Let's talk to the others.

15:51.960 --> 15:53.140
Yeah.

15:54.990 --> 15:56.820
I'm sorry I worried you.

15:56.820 --> 15:59.160
No, I'm the one who's sorry.

15:59.160 --> 16:02.130
I never would've guessed
it had been two weeks.

16:02.430 --> 16:05.890
That's why I went to see the prince
and borrow his Seeker's Compass.

16:06.330 --> 16:08.800
I knew you were alive,

16:08.800 --> 16:13.220
but I thought maybe you
couldn't find the exit.

16:13.220 --> 16:18.900
So I was hoping I could share the
direction it indicated with you somehow.

16:21.150 --> 16:22.530
Yuke... Yuke!

16:23.150 --> 16:25.390
That light... The voice!

16:25.390 --> 16:28.030
So that was you guiding me, huh?

16:28.920 --> 16:31.130
You really saved me, Rain.

16:31.130 --> 16:33.640
You're what led me back home.

16:33.640 --> 16:34.790
Thanks.

16:34.790 --> 16:37.070
I had faith in you.

16:37.070 --> 16:40.910
And since the prince agreed to my bet,

16:40.910 --> 16:44.050
I think he's a bit different
from other Salmutarians.

16:44.540 --> 16:45.760
Seems so.

16:45.760 --> 16:47.460
Yeah, which is why...

16:47.460 --> 16:48.760
I know.

16:48.760 --> 16:51.420
Let's try to figure out if
there's anything we can do.

16:51.420 --> 16:52.100
Yeah.

16:53.710 --> 16:54.560
Ow!

16:56.560 --> 16:58.600
Don't make me worry like that!

16:58.600 --> 17:00.320
S-Sorry...

17:00.700 --> 17:04.200
I'm glad Rain is safely back with us, too.

17:04.200 --> 17:06.070
Now our problems won't grow even bigger.

17:06.440 --> 17:08.950
I'm so glad you're okay, Rain!

17:09.320 --> 17:11.200
I'm glad you're okay, too.

17:11.790 --> 17:13.480
It's good to have you back.

17:13.480 --> 17:17.720
I'd like to hear everything that
happened, but you should rest first.

17:17.720 --> 17:18.460
I will.

17:18.460 --> 17:20.870
Good work conquering the dungeon,

17:20.870 --> 17:22.980
Hero Yuke Feldio.

17:22.980 --> 17:26.220
I'll be returning that
heavy label soon enough.

17:26.220 --> 17:30.220
The culling—Glad Shi-im—is entirely gone.

17:30.220 --> 17:32.420
I'll put a log together right away.

17:34.060 --> 17:39.160
Members of Clover, it seems your
leader is a bit of a workaholic.

17:39.160 --> 17:39.730
Huh?!

17:40.050 --> 17:43.470
Make sure he rests until
the time of the debriefing.

17:43.470 --> 17:45.640
If anything comes up, let the guild know.

17:45.640 --> 17:48.740
Don't let this idiot do more
than he needs to until then.

17:49.080 --> 17:50.360
You can count on us.

17:50.360 --> 17:51.810
We'll force him if we must!

17:52.430 --> 17:54.500
I swear it on Mamar's name!

17:55.010 --> 17:56.350
I'll watch him, too!

17:56.350 --> 17:57.090
Hey...

17:57.090 --> 17:58.900
I'll assist them, as well.

17:58.900 --> 18:00.130
Not you, too!

18:01.300 --> 18:02.880
I'll be taking my leave, then.

18:03.260 --> 18:06.380
I'll inform you of the date and
time of our debriefing later.

18:06.900 --> 18:09.260
You will rest. Got that?

18:09.260 --> 18:12.100
Y-Yes, ma'am...

18:12.830 --> 18:14.770
Thanks for the meal.

18:14.770 --> 18:19.330
I wouldn't call it a party,
but I hope it filled you up.

18:19.330 --> 18:22.150
It did. Thank you, Fina.

18:22.600 --> 18:26.400
We'll have a party next time, okay?

18:26.770 --> 18:29.420
Have you calmed down a bit, Master?

18:29.420 --> 18:33.510
Yeah. Sorry again for worrying all of you.

18:33.510 --> 18:34.840
I'm sorry.

18:34.840 --> 18:35.910
It's all right.

18:36.270 --> 18:38.910
Welcome back, Yuke, Rune.

18:38.910 --> 18:40.450
Welcome back!

18:41.780 --> 18:45.050
Well, Rune,
it's time for you to go to bed.

18:45.050 --> 18:47.290
What? I'm not tired yet!

18:47.290 --> 18:51.140
Too bad. Nene, see her to her room.

18:51.140 --> 18:51.930
Got it!

18:52.550 --> 18:53.900
Let's go.

18:55.260 --> 18:58.180
Marina, you take Master
to the hot spring.

18:58.180 --> 19:00.010
No, no! I can go by myself!

19:00.010 --> 19:02.330
Watch him to make sure he doesn't work.

19:02.330 --> 19:03.560
Okay!

19:03.560 --> 19:04.680
Well, let's go!

19:04.680 --> 19:07.440
Hey! Quit pulling!

19:07.440 --> 19:08.920
I'll go with—

19:10.350 --> 19:14.040
Rain, I still need to lecture
you for acting on your own,

19:14.040 --> 19:18.340
even if it was because you
were worried about Master.

19:24.230 --> 19:26.320
Um... Marina?

19:26.320 --> 19:27.260
Yes?

19:27.260 --> 19:29.550
What... is going on here?

19:29.550 --> 19:31.770
I'm keeping an eye on you.

19:31.770 --> 19:33.930
I-I told you I'd be fine!

19:33.930 --> 19:36.060
Well, I was really worried, you know.

19:36.060 --> 19:37.270
I know that...

19:37.270 --> 19:40.440
But could you, you know,
move away a little bit now?

19:40.440 --> 19:41.060
Nope.

19:42.010 --> 19:44.910
You have two weeks of attention
to make up for.

19:46.050 --> 19:47.990
Hey! You gave up!

19:47.990 --> 19:52.200
I'm the one giving you all the attention!
You're not giving me any!

19:52.510 --> 19:55.130
All right, Princess, what is your demand?

19:55.130 --> 19:57.100
Well, when you put it that way...

19:57.100 --> 19:59.450
Ask for anything.
I worried you, after all.

19:59.770 --> 20:02.560
I can't come up with something
on the spot, though.

20:02.560 --> 20:06.260
Um... I can really ask for anything?

20:06.260 --> 20:08.210
Anything I can do, at least.

20:08.570 --> 20:12.430
Okay, then... I'm gonna ask now. Ready?

20:12.430 --> 20:13.370
Sure.

20:13.370 --> 20:14.760
Are you really sure?

20:14.760 --> 20:16.470
Trust me.

20:22.280 --> 20:24.570
Wh-What?! That's...

20:24.570 --> 20:26.580
You said I could ask anything!

20:26.580 --> 20:27.730
I did, but...

20:27.730 --> 20:31.240
Okay, fine! That's what you want, right?!

20:31.240 --> 20:32.740
Really? You'll do it?

20:32.740 --> 20:34.850
A leader keeps his promises!

20:34.850 --> 20:37.900
Yay! I can't wait!

20:40.620 --> 20:41.700
Rune?!

20:41.700 --> 20:44.050
No fair for you to get him
all to yourself!

20:44.050 --> 20:45.870
I'm gonna bathe with him, too!

20:45.870 --> 20:49.680
Hey! Rune, we told you
it was your bedtime!

20:49.680 --> 20:51.850
Get in with us, Nene!

20:51.850 --> 20:52.380
Wha—

20:52.380 --> 20:54.880
Yeah, jump in! Get the others, too!

20:56.200 --> 20:57.390
Got it!

21:02.390 --> 21:04.640
Doesn't this feel great, Yuke?

21:04.640 --> 21:06.270
Doesn't it, Yuke?

21:06.270 --> 21:08.770
It's relaxing, isn't it, Master?

21:08.770 --> 21:12.400
Having a bath with everyone
is pretty nice, huh, Yuke?

21:12.680 --> 21:16.810
Hey, you're bright red! Are you okay?

21:16.810 --> 21:18.230
Did you overheat?

21:20.110 --> 21:22.300
Wow, he really is red!

21:22.300 --> 21:23.780
He sure is!

22:55.920 --> 22:57.050
(The Seven-Leaf Clover)

22:57.050 --> 22:59.840
(The Seven-Leaf Clover)
Next time, "The Seven-Leaf Clover."

22:59.840 --> 23:00.930
(The Seven-Leaf Clover)
